I would keep this as your VISION.md. Then I'd create separate documents for implementation, for example:

VISION.md → The long-term mission (the document above)
ARCHITECTURE.md → Technical architecture, database schema, APIs, authentication, security
UI_UX.md → Design system, branding, colors, typography, components
AI.md → AI search, RAG, prompts, moderation, vector search
SEO.md → URL structure, Schema.org, internal linking, content strategy
ROADMAP.md → Milestones, priorities, feature backlog
AGENTS.md → Responsibilities for each Claude coding agent and coding standards
BRAND.md → Logo, voice, messaging, visual identity
RULES.md → Development principles, security rules, performance budgets, naming conventions

That structure will scale much better than one giant file and gives Claude (or other AI coding agents) clear boundaries for each part of the project.

